// crates: push every crate onto a target.
//
// A puzzle game for the terminal that combines several features:
// - Puzzles are text files, found with $listDir and read with $readFile; a
//   file with a mistake is reported and skipped.
// - The board is a grid of terrain (lib/grid.wvt), with the crates in a map
//   keyed by position (§10.11).
// - It is drawn in layers with lib/view.wvt: in colour in a terminal, with
//   targets that shimmer while the game waits for a key ($waitKey), and as
//   plain text when the output is not a terminal ($terminal).
// - Undo keeps the earlier states in an array.
//
// Arrow keys, h j k l or w a s d move; u undoes, r restarts, n and p go to the
// next and previous puzzle, and q or Escape quits.
//
// Usage: wvc build samples/crates.wvt, then run it in a terminal. The puzzles
// are in crates-puzzles/ next to the program, or in the folder given as its
// argument.
//
// A puzzle file uses the usual text layout: # wall, a space floor, . target,
// $ crate, * crate on a target, @ player, + player on a target. A line that
// starts with ; is a comment, and "; title: ..." names the puzzle.

;import grid from "$lib/grid.wvt"
;import view from "$lib/view.wvt"
;import text from "$lib/text.wvt"
;import math from "$lib/math.wvt"

;enum Terrain (floor, wall, target)

